WHAT YOU ARE INSTALLING:\par
\par
  \u8226?  Ninety.exe \u8212? the application interface and controller.\par
  \u8226?  sing-box.exe \u8212? the primary networking engine.\par
  \u8226?  xray.exe \u8212? the engine used for XHTTP connections.\par
  \u8226?  naive.exe and trusttunnel_client.exe \u8212? local protocol bridges for\par
     NaiveProxy and TrustTunnel.\par
  \u8226?  wintun.dll \u8212? the virtual network adapter component for VPN \u183? TUN mode.\par
  \u8226?  winws.exe, WinDivert64.sys and Monkey64.sys \u8212? DPI-bypass components.\par
\par
Ninety does not install its own permanently running Windows service.\par
Elevated access is requested only for operations that require it: VPN \u183? TUN,\par
DPI bypass and cleanup of the corresponding drivers.\par
\par
WHAT IS SENT TO THE INTERNET:\par
\par
  \u8226?  Subscriptions are fetched from addresses added by the user. When direct\par
     fallback refresh is enabled, the request may be made without the VPN.\par
  \u8226?  VPN traffic is sent to user-selected servers and their network providers.\par
  \u8226?  App updates are checked through GitLab and GitHub Releases; DPI data is\par
     updated through a signed GitHub Releases channel.\par
  \u8226?  Region, availability and connection-quality checks contact external test\par
     or IP services only when the corresponding features are used.\par
  \u8226?  WARP registration contacts the Cloudflare API only on explicit request.\par
  \u8226?  Ninety contains no first-party telemetry, analytics or advertising.\par
